steps {
  type: CORTEX_STEP_TYPE_USER_INPUT
  status: CORTEX_STEP_STATUS_DONE
  metadata {
    created_at {
      seconds: 1791917391
      nanos: 101441710
    }
    source: CORTEX_STEP_SOURCE_USER_EXPLICIT
    source_trajectory_step_info {
      trajectory_id: "1af327b4-31de-4d28-8059-9ddf5c4831ba"
      step_index: 1
      cascade_id: "1af327b4-31de-4d28-8059-9ddf5c4831ba"
    }
  }
  user_input {
    user_response: "# GOOGLE AI STUDIO PROMPT: AI ACADEMY AND TECHNOLOGY GUIDE\n\n## 1. App Overview\n\nCreate a complete Android application named **AI Academy \342\200\224 AI Technology Guide** using Kotlin and Jetpack Compose.\n\nThe application is an educational reference guide that introduces users to modern AI technologies, tools, frameworks, platforms, and infrastructure.\n\nIts primary purpose is to help users understand what each technology is, what it does, how it is commonly used, and how it differs from other technologies.\n\n**Important:** This app should focus on concise, informative descriptions. Do not create lengthy step-by-step tutorials, installation walkthroughs, extensive code examples, or complicated technical courses.\n\n## 2. Technology Stack\n\nUse:\n- Kotlin\n- Jetpack Compose\n- Material 3\n- Navigation Compose\n- MVVM architecture\n- Room Database or DataStore for saving bookmarks and learning progress, where appropriate.\n\nThe application must work offline using bundled educational content. No AI API key, paid database, or account registration should be required.\n\n## 3. App Design\n\nCreate a modern, professional, mobile-friendly interface with:\n- Dark navy, blue, and violet accents.\n- Light and dark themes.\n- Clean typography and readable text.\n- Modern technology cards and category icons.\n- Search and filtering.\n- Consistent navigation.\n- Responsive layouts.\n\nApp title: **AI Academy**\n\nSubtitle: *Explore the World of Artificial Intelligence*\n\n## 4. Main Navigation\n\nCreate five bottom navigation tabs:\n\n1. **Home** \342\200\224 welcome section, featured categories, and recently viewed technologies.\n2. **Explore** \342\200\224 all AI categories and their technologies.\n3. **Search** \342\200\224 search technologies by name, category, or description.\n4. **Bookmarks** \342\200\224 saved technologies.\n5. **Settings** \342\200\224 theme selection, app information, and preferences.\n\n## 5. Required AI Categories and Technologies\n\nInclude all eleven categories and every technology listed below.\n\n### A. Large Language Models (LLMs)\n- OpenAI GPT\n- Anthropic Claude\n- Google Gemini\n- Meta Llama\n- Mistral AI\n- Cohere\n- Hugging Face\n- Ollama\n- vLLM\n\n### B. Agentic AI Frameworks\n- LangGraph\n- CrewAI\n- Microsoft AutoGen\n- Microsoft Agent Framework\n- LlamaIndex Workflows\n- AWS Strands Agents\n- CAMEL\n- Agno\n\n### C. Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG)\n- LangChain\n- LlamaIndex\n- Haystack\n- DSPy\n- RAGFlow\n- GraphRAG\n- Unstructured\n- EmbedChain\n\n### D. Embedding Models\n- OpenAI Embeddings\n- Cohere Embed\n- Voyage AI\n- Sentence Transformers\n- BGE\n- Google Vertex AI Embeddings\n- Azure OpenAI Embeddings\n\n### E. Model Context Protocol (MCP)\n- MCP SDK\n- FastMCP\n- MCP Registry\n- GitHub MCP Server\n- Slack MCP Server\n- PostgreSQL MCP Server\n- Google Drive MCP Server\n- Filesystem MCP Server\n\n### F. AI Security and Guardrails\n- NVIDIA NeMo Guardrails\n- Guardrails AI\n- Microsoft Presidio\n- Lakera Guard\n- Prompt Security\n- Protect AI\n- Azure AI Content Safety\n- AWS Bedrock Guardrails\n\n### G. AI Observability and Evaluation\n- LangSmith\n- Langfuse\n- Arize Phoenix\n- Weights & Biases Weave\n- TruLens\n- Ragas\n- Promptfoo\n- Helicone\n\n### H. AI Memory Systems\n- Mem0\n- Zep\n- Letta\n- LangGraph Memory\n- Redis\n- PostgreSQL\n- Neo4j\n- Chroma\n\n### I. AI Agent SDKs and Platforms\n- OpenAI Agents SDK\n- LangChain Agents\n- PydanticAI\n- Semantic Kernel\n- Google ADK\n- AWS Bedrock Agents\n- Azure AI Foundry Agent Service\n\n### J. AI Workflow Automation\n- n8n\n- Zapier\n- Make\n- Microsoft Power Automate\n- Temporal\n- Apache Airflow\n- Prefect\n- Kestra\n- Pipedream\n\n### K. Vector Databases and Vector Search\n- Pinecone\n- Weaviate\n- Qdrant\n- Milvus\n- Chroma\n- pgvector\n- Elasticsearch\n- Redis\n- MongoDB Atlas Vector Search\n\n## 6. Technology Description Format\n\nEvery technology must have its own dedicated information page.\n\nKeep each description concise, clear, and informative. Use the following format:\n\n**1. Technology Name**\n\nDisplay the official or commonly recognized name.\n\n**2. Overview**\n\nWrite a short paragraph explaining what the technology is.\n\n**3. Main Purpose**\n\nExplain what problem it solves or what it is designed to do.\n\n**4. Key Features**\n\nList three to five important capabilities.\n\n**5. Common Uses**\n\nList two to four practical situations where the technology is used.\n\n**6. Advantages**\n\nBriefly explain its main strengths.\n\n**7. Limitations**\n\nMention important trade-offs or considerations.\n\n**8. Related Technologies**\n\nList relevant technologies from the app that users may want to explore next.\n\n**9. Official Website**\n\nProvide a verified official website or documentation link when available.\n\nEach technology page should generally contain approximately 100\342\200\223200 words, excluding short feature lists and links. Use simpler explanations for straightforward tools and slightly more detail when necessary to explain complex concepts.\n\nDo not force every entry to have identical wording or artificially inflate descriptions.\n\n## 7. Home Screen\n\nCreate a functional dashboard containing:\n- App name and welcome message.\n- Search bar.\n- Eleven category cards.\n- Total number of listed technologies.\n- Recently viewed technologies.\n- Bookmarked technologies.\n- Featured AI technology of the day, selected from bundled content.\n- A short explanation of what AI Academy offers.\n\nSelecting a category must open its technology list. Selecting a technology must open its description page.\n\n## 8. Category Pages\n\nEach category page must include:\n- Category name.\n- Short category overview.\n- Its complete list of technologies.\n- A concise explanation of the category\'s purpose.\n- Search or filtering within the category.\n- Technology cards showing the name and a short description.\n\nDisplay all technologies using a clean, scrollable layout.\n\n## 9. Search Functionality\n\nImplement working offline search across:\n- Technology names.\n- Category names.\n- Technology descriptions.\n- Main purposes.\n- Features and common uses.\n\nAllow users to filter results by category.\n\nSearch results must open the correct technology information page.\n\n## 10. Bookmarks and Recently Viewed\n\nAllow users to:\n- Bookmark and remove bookmarks.\n- View saved technologies.\n- See recently viewed technologies.\n- Retain bookmarks and preferences after closing and reopening the app.\n\nUse local persistence. A user account or remote database is unnecessary.\n\n## 11. Educational Accuracy\n\nWrite original, factual, beginner-friendly descriptions.\n\nClearly distinguish between:\n- LLM providers and individual model families.\n- Model hosting and inference engines.\n- AI agent frameworks and managed agent services.\n- RAG frameworks and document-processing tools.\n- Embedding models and embedding services.\n- MCP infrastructure and MCP servers.\n- AI security products and general-purpose validation tools.\n- Observability platforms and evaluation frameworks.\n- Memory frameworks and general-purpose databases.\n- Workflow automation platforms and durable workflow orchestration systems.\n- Vector databases and traditional databases with vector-search capabilities.\n\nDo not imply that every technology in a category performs exactly the same function.\n\nUse current official documentation when verifying technology descriptions and links. Avoid unsupported claims about pricing, free usage, licenses, or specific features.\n\n## 12. Technical Requirements\n\n- All eleven categories must be present.\n- Every listed technology must have its own description page.\n- All buttons and navigation must work.\n- All initial content must be available offline.\n- Search must work without an internet connection.\n- Bookmarks must persist locally.\n- Support light and dark themes.\n- Use appropriate Android back navigation.\n- Provide useful empty states.\n- Use stable identifiers for categories and technologies.\n- Do not add unnecessary permissions or require API keys.\n- Do not implement a fake AI chatbot or pretend to provide live AI services.\n\nInclude a clean project structure, README.md, `.gitignore`, and basic tests for navigation, search, and content completeness.\n\n## 13. Scope Restrictions\n\nThis application is a descriptive AI technology guide, not a programming course.\n\nDo not add:\n- Lengthy step-by-step tutorials.\n- Detailed installation instructions.\n- Full programming courses.\n- Large code samples.\n- Complex interactive coding environments.\n- Mandatory online AI integrations.\n- Unnecessary authentication.\n- Paid database dependencies.\n\nKeep the application lightweight, informative, easy to navigate, and useful for discovering and comparing AI technologies.\n\n## 14. Final Deliverable\n\nGenerate a functional Android Studio project using Kotlin and Jetpack Compose.\n\nImplement the complete user interface, all eleven categories, every listed technology, concise educational descriptions, verified official links, offline search, bookmarks, recently viewed technologies, local persistence, and theme settings.\n\nDo not stop at a mockup or sample screen. Generate the actual application files, verify the project where possible, and provide instructions for opening, building, and running the app in Android Studio.\n\n**Final instruction:** Prioritize complete technology coverage, accurate descriptions, simple navigation, and a polished user experience over technical complexity or lengthy tutorials.\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_START]\nInstructions: If you need more context from the user you must first ask the user some questions using the ask_question tool. If you ask questions, you must wait for the user\'s answers. After the questions you must present a plan.\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_END]"
    items {
